Show
/ Shows an error: the template for its status code in this folder renders it, and it is written to
/ the error channel. The caller hands the error in by name — `call /system/error/Show error=%!error%`
/ inside a handler; at the top level the app hands in the failed run's error.
- set %template% = "/system/error/%error.StatusCode%.txt"
- render %template%, error=%error%, on error 404 call Fallback then retry once, write to %text%
- write %text% to error channel

Fallback
/ No template for this code: its family's — 400.txt below 500, 500.txt from 500 up.
- set %template% = "/system/error/400.txt"
- if %error.StatusCode% >= 500, call Runtime

Runtime
- set %template% = "/system/error/500.txt"
